From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Jul 2023 10:27:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: stop an overlapping background chain at CAC start

When the main chain starts a CAC on a channel that the background
chain covers, the background chain has nothing left to prepare there.

cfg80211 now stops the background chain in that case, so that its
owner can move it to another channel. This covers a chain in CAC and
a chain that finished its CAC and only monitors the channel. The
chain stops before cfg80211 marks the CAC on the subchannels, because
the abort of the chain clears that mark on the subchannels it shares
with the new CAC.

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/wireless/nl80211.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/net/wireless/nl80211.c
+++ b/net/wireless/nl80211.c
@@ -11975,6 +11975,12 @@ static int nl80211_start_radar_detection
 	wdev->links[link_id].cac_started = true;
 	wdev->links[link_id].cac_start_time = jiffies;
 	wdev->links[link_id].cac_time_ms = cac_time_ms;
+
+	if (rdev->background_radar_wdev &&
+	    cfg80211_is_sub_chan(&chandef, rdev->background_radar_chandef.chan, false)) {
+		cfg80211_stop_background_radar_detection(rdev->background_radar_wdev);
+	}
+
 	cfg80211_set_cac_state(wiphy, &chandef, true);
 
 	return 0;
